Ported from the SDR Workbench's decoders (Apache-2.0, same authors).

- Jonathan Olds, Copyright 2015-2019: JAERO (https://github.com/jontio/JAERO, MIT License).
  src/aero.c follows JAERO's Aero P-channel scrambler, interleaver, CRC, frame layouts (10.5k and
  600/1200 bit/s), ISU/SSU reassembly and ACARS parsing. src/msk.c (the MSK demodulator) is
  original to this project.
- STD-C (src/stdc.c) was written from the published frame structure; its protocol constants were
  checked against inmarsat-sniffer (GPL-3.0), used only as a reference: no code was copied.
- libacars-2 (Tomasz Lemiech, MIT License) decodes ACARS applications when linked.
- libairspy and libhackrf (BSD 3-Clause) drive the USB receivers when linked.
